rust-proxmox-sendmail (1.0.4-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * fix #7814: normalize line endings of sent and forwarded mail to CRLF
    and drop bare CR bytes, as SMTP does not allow bare CR or LF. This
    no longer depends on the local MTA to convert line endings.

  * strip all control characters from attachment filenames to avoid
    compatibility issues with mail clients.

  * add a public helper to normalize line endings, so that code sending
    mail by other means, like the SMTP notification target, can apply
    the same normalization.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 20:51:45 +0100

